WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.669
-Our next guest is a very
talented actress you know from

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.704
shows such as "Ray Donovan"
and "Better Call Saul."

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:07.407
She stars in
"The Banshees of Inisherin,"

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.675
which is in select theaters now.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.942
Let's take a look.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:11.544
-What are you doing home?

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.878
-I knocked on
Colm's sonny lorry.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.180
He was just sitting there.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.349
-Sitting there doing what?

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:20.319
-Sitting there doing nothing,
smoking.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:21.453
-Was he asleep?

00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:23.156
-He was smoking, Siobhan.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.957
How do you smoke
in your sleep, like?

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.826
-Have you been rowing?

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.928
-We haven't been rowing.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.899
I don't think we've been rowing.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.536
Have we been rowing?

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.476
Why wouldn't he
answer the door to me?

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:47.146
-Maybe he just doesn't
like you no more.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:50.483
-Please welcome to the show
Kerry Condon, everyone.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.519
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.367
Kerry, how are you?

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.835
-Hey, hi. I'm a bit nervous.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.136
It's my first
talk show in America.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.571
-Well, you're off to
a great start.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.772
You fully got up to the chair,
and that's the hardest part.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.407
-Yeah, I know.
I was worried about that.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.674
Thank you.
-Yeah. Now it's a breeze.

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.343
From here on out, it's a breeze.
-Thank you.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.945
-I'm a huge fan of yours.
I love this movie.

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:21.514
For those who don't know,
it's about a couple of friends

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.648
who break up.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.117
It's a platonic-breakup film.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.786
You play the sister of
Colin Farrell's character.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.420
You've worked with Colin before.
-Yes.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.489
-In a film called
"Intermission," I believe.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.924
-Yes.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.359
-Yeah. And, so, was it nice to
have a sort of reunion of sorts?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.593
-It was.

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:36.729
I'd known him over the years,
like, you know,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.332
seeing him at things and stuff
and texts and things like that.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.001
So, it is, because when
someone's quite famous,

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.537
you know, I'm always a bit
nervous about imposing on them.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.672
And, like, you know, people are
always coming up to them,

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:47.973
and I don't want to be
that person

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:49.375
who's always coming up to them.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.043
So, I think if it
had been someone else,

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:54.246
it would have been a bit --
taking my time approaching him,

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.482
where it was easy
because I knew him for so long.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:59.084
-He's a pretty approachable --
As far as a famous person goes,

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:00.719
I do find -- I think Colin's a
pretty approachable fella.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:03.523
-Yeah, but, still, you don't
want to be annoying people.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.924
You know what I mean?
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.660
That's a good lesson here
for everyone here to take away.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.030
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:15.301
Now, this was shot on an island
off the coast of Ireland.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.069
And, you know,
Brendan and Colin were here,

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.571
and they were talking about
the locals

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.072
and their varying levels
of excitement

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:21.840
of having a movie
filmed on their island.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.310
Did you find that people
were excited to see

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.345
either you or Brendan or Colin?

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.947
-Well, no, the only people
who were excited

00:02:28.947 --> 00:02:32.018
where I was living were
these two cute little boys,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.653
who were, like,
really, really young.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.521
And all of them
had cute little glasses.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.057
And they knew Brendan from
"Paddington."

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:41.160
-Yeah.
-Oh, my God! It was so cute!

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.295
-And did they care about
Colin at all?

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.130
-Couldn't give a
[bleep] about Colin, yeah.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.431
-Well, there you go.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.498
Well, that will keep
him from getting, you know --

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:47.699
getting airs about him,
you know?

00:02:47.699 --> 00:02:51.170
-Exactly. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.172
-You know, even in the clip,
we saw, I guess,

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.174
a little Shetland pony there.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.909
-A little donkey.
-A little donkey, right.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.410
Excuse me.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.879
A correction that's made in the
film, as well, I should note.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.280
-Yes.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.550
-It didn't seem like you had
to do as much of the sort of

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.219
animal co-starring that
Colin had to do.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.954
But did you find that you spent
a fair amount of time,

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.723
more than normal, with animals?

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.091
-Yeah, well,
I'm good with animals

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.927
because I've got
horses of my own, you know?

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.994
So I'd be good around them.

00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:19.432
But Jenny, the little donkey --
she was very young,

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:23.436
and, so, she had a little friend
donkey with her all the time.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.571
Yes! Called Rosie.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:27.907
-So, is that because
when you're young on set,

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:29.408
there are rules,
like, the donkey union --

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:32.412
-Like a chaperone, yes.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.013
And then Rosie
would come on the set

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.115
and be, like,
kind of an older presence.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.217
And so Jenny
would kind of relax a bit more

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.718
when she could see Rosie.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:42.754
So I really, like -- Yeah, it
made Rosie feel really special,

00:03:42.754 --> 00:03:44.323
'cause I hate favoritism.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:45.357
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:46.659
-And it can happen.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.361
It can happen with animals
just as easy

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.862
as is it can
with the cast, yeah.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.896
And it's very nice
to have someone

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:52.264
who's sort of familiar
with horses.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.366
to notice which one's
getting the favoritism.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:57.002
'Cause it seemed Colin
didn't enjoy the horses as much.

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:58.838
-He had to a scene --
He had to do loads of

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.973
horse-and-carrot stuff,
which is hard, now,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.075
and I'm not good at that.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.709
But, like, he knew I had horses,

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:07.179
so I suppose he was
a little maybe insecure.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.648
doing the horse stuff.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.416
But I always tried to leave him
alone when he was doing it

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.518
so he wouldn't be embarrassed
or anything.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.087
But we did have one day when we
were quite close to a cliff,

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:16.656
and I think the horse was
getting a bit, by the end of it,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.024
like, "I'm done.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.626
I just am done with this.
I don't want to do it anymore."

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:23.129
And it was windy and all sorts.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:26.098
And at the end of the take,
Colin said to the costume lady,

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.701
"Oh, can I have a change of
underpants, please?"

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:35.474
Because we nearly went into
the -- off the cliff, yeah.

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:38.277
-It is -- This movie takes
place, you know,

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.346
100 years ago or so.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.347
But, yet, it feels
very modern in the themes.

00:04:42.347 --> 00:04:43.549
And it's also very funny.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.451
I know you've worked with
Martin over the years.

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.420
And, you know, he's written --

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.654
He obviously writes in
different eras.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.690
But I do feel like
there's this very --

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.524
like, a DNA that goes
through all his writing,

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.660
where it's very easy to
listen to.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.562
It's very funny.
It does seem very natural.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.732
Was it fun to get to work with
a script like this?

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:03.335
-Yeah, because I always loved
his Irish stuff.

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:04.937
Like, I mean,
I was a little biased --

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.105
-Now, you're Irish, correct?

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.774
-Yes, of course.
-Yeah, okay.

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:10.643
-And I had done all
the Irish plays,

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:13.212
so they were, like,
what I liked about his stuff,

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.714
and I always felt like
they were very moving.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.683
And when he'd done his movies,
I was thinking,

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.685
"Oh, people, like, they haven't
seen all his stuff,"

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.654
because the Irish stuff
was so great.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.856
So when I read the script,
I remember thinking, "Oh, yes!

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.391
It's like one of your
Irish plays but a movie,

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:29.362
so everyone's going to see now
how great you are at that,

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.597
the dialogue of the Irish stuff.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.933
-It's a wonderful cast
from top to bottom.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.202
And, obviously, this was shot at
a time where people

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.303
weren't getting
to interact as much

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.671
because it was during COVID.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.073
And it -- I can only imagine
how nice it must have been

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.276
to be amongst a group of actors
who were working on

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.011
something as special as this is.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:47.446
-Yeah, I hate talking about
COVID, though.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.949
-Yeah, we don't have to.
-I hate it. I'm so sick of it.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.016
Isn't that terrible?

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.985
But it's like
I think I have PTSD.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.554
I shouldn't say that,
'cause I don't really have PTSD.

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.356
But there's something about it.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:58.825
I just, like --
I wish we just never --

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.459
Pretend it never happened.
-You know what?

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:01.994
Let's just pretend
it never happened, alright?

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:03.396
-Thank you.
-You're very welcome.

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.497
-Thank you.

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:07.066
-If you ever see a photo of me
wearing a mask,

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.300
it's because I had a bad cold.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.368
-Yay. Okay, okay.
-It was a cold.

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:11.137
It was nothing else.

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:14.073
You were on one of
my favorite shows,

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.507
which was "Better Call Saul."

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:19.111
And you came in,
but you had never seen

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:20.779
"Breaking Bad," correct?

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:23.915
-Yeah. God almighty.
I'll never live that down.

00:06:23.915 --> 00:06:26.953
I saw it now, but I hadn't seen
it when I did my --

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.621
-That's okay.
-Yeah, because it was a prequel.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.689
-Yeah.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.256
-Like, in my defense,
it was a prequel.

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:32.325
So I was like, "Well,
I don't really need to know

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.725
what happens in the future."

00:06:33.725 --> 00:06:36.162
-Yeah. In a weird way,

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:37.930
it would make the job
as an actor harder.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.899
because your character shouldn't
know what the future is.

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:43.035
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:44.436
Look at me making up
excuses for you.

00:06:44.436 --> 00:06:46.905
-Well, I know, for my laziness.
I know.

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:48.340
It wasn't laziness.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:52.511
I think I didn't know what
the audition was for, I believe.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.813
-Well, you shouldn't have to go
watch seven seasons of a show

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:55.881
before an audition.

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:58.785
-I mean, you know --
-Yeah, I do.

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:00.686
Now, by the way, I didn't even
get a call for the audition,

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.821
so who am I to say?

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.689
-Well, I did
watch it eventually,

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.157
and I'm glad
I didn't watch it before,

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:06.892
'cause I think I would
have been really nervous,

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:09.628
because it was so good
and it was so original.

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.164
And I think I
would have overthought it.

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.998
So I was kind of glad
I hadn't seen it.

00:07:12.998 --> 00:07:14.199
-Well, I said it to everybody
who worked on

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:15.434
"Better Call Saul."

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.403
Like, another thing that
I couldn't believe worked,

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.839
but not only worked, but it was
exactly as good as the original.

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:20.940
So it was a really
cool thing to see.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.274
It was great to see you in it.

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:23.976
But this film, you were so
wonderful in this film.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.277
-Thanks a million.

00:07:25.277 --> 00:07:27.480
-And I told Brendan and Colin
when they were here,

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.647
because they're two of
my favorite actors,

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.016
but when they
were in scenes with you,

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:31.451
you were just
running circles around them.

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.352
So thank you so much
for being here.

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.153
-Thanks a million.
Thank you so much.

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.723
-I really appreciate it.
Kerry Condon, everybody.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.293
"The Banshees of Inisherin"
in select theaters now.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.860
We'll be right back
with music from

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.396
Kurt Vile &amp; the Violators.

